From 91eaaa59e1ba5d66516e2db6269be58d733c3692 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:11:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Late admission: decide each step when the step in flight
 reaches a decoder layer

With async scheduling the engine core decides step N+1 as soon as step N is
under way and launches it behind N. A request that arrives while N runs is
read only after N's output, when N+1 is already fixed, so it joins N+2 and
waits one whole step for nothing. On DS4.1 TP3 (r6x) a traced replay shows
every short request waiting exactly one such step: 62 ms of a 258 ms time to
first token at four streams, 97 of 352 ms at eight.

VLLM_LATE_ADMISSION_LAYER=K moves the decision later without giving up what
async scheduling hides. A forward pre-hook on decoder layer K records one CUDA
event; in a full CUDA graph the record is captured as an external event node,
so every replay records it as it reaches the layer. The V2 runner's
execute_model returns an asynchronous reply that waits on that event, so the
output rank's reply reaches the engine core when the step reaches layer K, in
order before the step's sampled output. The engine core waits for the reply
of the step in flight, takes the requests that arrived meanwhile, and only then
decides the next step. Layers K and later, sampling and drafting still hide
the decision and the next step's preparation. An idle engine decides at once;
a step without a forward replies at once. The default, -1, keeps today's
behaviour. Requires async scheduling without pipeline parallelism (startup
error otherwise).

Base: local-inference-lab integration/karmic-kraken-beta 19f2c20e + the r6x
series (7316c7f9f).

Quality: no tensor is read or written; the event only orders the host's
decision. Which requests share a step changes, which batch invariance already
covers (temperature-0 outputs identical in any batch).

Tests: tests/v1/engine/test_late_admission.py (an arrival during a step joins
the next step with late admission and the one after without; no wait with
nothing in flight; startup checks; the engine process admits every queued
request without blocking) and tests/v1/worker/test_late_admission.py (the
event is recorded as layer K starts, for a causal LM and DS4.1's vision
wrapper; refused layers; the reply waits for the event and carries nothing;
WorkerProc sends it once the event completes; on a GPU, a captured graph
records the event at the layer on every replay while later layers still run).

Upstream status: local; not proposed.
